    {
      "id": "IA-01",
      "finding": "C restores types and roles but also changes word count and lexical specificity; this is a fixed-query observational comparison, not isolated causal identification of role nouns."
    },
    {
      "id": "IA-02",
      "finding": "P1 C1 is a selection alignment criterion, not transfer-causes-interoperability claim."
    },
    {
      "id": "IA-03",
      "finding": "P2 has generic governance recommendations rather than a live deployment owner deciding; generalization to software component search is limited."
    },
    {
      "id": "IA-04",
      "finding": "P3 canonical identifier and immutable target are distinct; neither source $schema URI spelling nor HTTP reachability establishes immutable returned content."
    },
    {
      "id": "IA-05",
      "finding": "B retains generic relations/labels (parts, rules, identifiers); perfect absence of all object nouns is not claimed."
    },
    {
